<title>LEBANON: Beirut bourse to halt banks' bloc deals.</title>
<headline>Beirut bourse to halt banks' bloc deals.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Beirut Stock Exchange (BSE) on Tuesday said it would halt bloc trading of Bank Audi, Bank of Beirut and Banque Libanais pour le Commerce shares from next Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The Beirut Stock Exchange has decided it will halt direct (bloc) transactions...(for the three banks),&quot; a statement said.</p>
<p>The freeze on the three banks' bloc deals would begin on Monday morning, it said.</p>
<p>BSE trading and information manager Fouad Baalbaki told Reuters the banks' stocks &quot;are very liquid and we prefer that they be put on the central market.&quot;</p>
<p>He said the freeze on bloc trading for the banks would be in force from Monday &quot;until further notice.&quot;</p>
</text>
